  "note": "Triennial election of the councillors of Londonderry Corporation, polled Wednesday 18 May 1949 (the aldermanships were not included). The Unionist nominees for the North Ward were returned unopposed on nomination day, 4 May (Derry Journal, 6 May 1949, p. 5); the Irish Labour Party contested the South and Waterside wards. Result: Anti-Partitionists 7 seats instead of 4; Unionist control retained. Hegarty's and Hamill's votes from the News-Letter and Irish News (illegible in the Journal's OCR). Cochrane, a former member, replaced Councillor R. Graham, who did not stand (News-Letter)."
